## 2. Multi-version build matrix (commit 2)
- `lib/cyrus/matrix` has four parts:
  - planMatrix: per version, the emitter, JDK, compile API, pack format, limits and pin; refusals come with reasons.
  - runMatrix: builds one version at a time; a failure stays on its own row; Test Flight runs per version.
  - matrixSummary: one plain sentence for the user.
  - pickForServer: built on lifecycle checkCompat; it never picks a blocked version.
- Flag `CYRUS_BUILD_MATRIX`. Not wired into the builds route yet, and the matrix record is not stored yet.
- **RAN** (no AI): one design, compiled per version against each pinned Paper server's own classpath (I made the 1.21.1/1.21.4/1.21.8 classpaths on node-2), then one flight per version. 1.21.1, 1.21.4, 1.21.8 and 1.21.11 passed. 26.2 was refused because it is a preview version (`matrix-r35-flights-2026-10-11.json`).

## 3. Try It throwaway server (commit 3)
- Controller `services/modbuilder/tools/tryit/tryit.js` on node-2. Each session is one transient systemd unit running as uid 65534, with:
  - a TTL of 30 min at most;
  - MemoryMax 1536M, CPU 200%, TasksMax 256;
  - a reap timer that removes it even if the portal never calls stop;
  - 1 session per user, 1 per host, 3 per user per day;
  - the whitelist on from the first tick;
